Install per user on Windows, without administrator rights

Hallow installs into %LOCALAPPDATA%\Hallow and registers itself for the
current user (HKCU), like Firefox does for users without administrator
rights. Neither the installer nor updates ever show a UAC prompt, and
updates need no privileged service: Gecko's updater, running as the user,
can replace the files.

- The installer never asks for elevation; even an elevated installer,
  uninstaller or post-update helper registers Hallow in HKCU.
- The installer sends no installation ping to Mozilla's telemetry, and
  launcher-process telemetry starts disabled; the uninstaller sends no
  uninstall ping and offers neither Mozilla's uninstall survey nor
  Firefox's profile refresh (which links to Mozilla's support site).
- Hallow, not Mozilla, is the publisher shown in Settings > Apps, and the
  self-extractor's window is titled Hallow (app.tag).

